#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087529 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087832 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "19d1448c-d5fd-5615-b657-ff4d66867834" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/id #uuid "67da2ffa-b472-5084-985c-dde4cd2df661" :question/math-academy-id "e-5219" :question/problem "What is the equation of the ellipse given below?\n\n![](images/57/57ec3c089f80e2d35d9b83f6791eefca9b452d933f82209ed434d35d77b78788.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{{a}^2}+\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{{b}^2}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(1,-1),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=5,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087532 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087833 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/id #uuid "e01914e2-b4f0-52b5-baf1-8b7fa5da3f18" :question/math-academy-id "e-5222" :question/problem "What is the equation of the ellipse given below?\n\n![](images/b6/b6eb2c0222181eaa4eb2a1c232fdf2eee905ab0e0a8a9c2284911ab8dd26cade.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{{a}^2}+\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{{b}^2}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-1,-3),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-1))^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-3))^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087533 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087834 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/id #uuid "10dda4fa-e047-53f4-a20a-b881e14f3e2a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5223" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\dfrac{(x-2)^2}{25} + \\dfrac{(y+2)^2}{16} = 1,$ find its center, and the lengths of its major and minor axes." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{{a}^2}+\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{{b}^2}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=2$ and $k=-2,$ so the center is located at $(2,-2).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have $a^2=25$ and $b^2=16.$\n\n- Since $a^2=25,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{25} = 5.$\n\n- Since $b^2=16,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{16} = 4.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=5,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=4.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a = 2\\cdot5 = 10,$ and the minor axis has length $2b = 2\\cdot4 = 8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435413 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087833 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a520ba4-1bc5-52a1-8b92-4fc8f8534ee4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{5}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435396} {:answer/id #uuid "9d0bb612-0c9d-520f-8d2d-1cd458c72942" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435401} {:answer/id #uuid "d3edf35a-4f87-5270-a7f9-9191deeedcf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435403} {:answer/id #uuid "f2f00129-bfef-5325-bde1-618b368cc3e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435406} {:answer/id #uuid "f94ac654-4ebc-5c1d-bd20-dcd10dcce606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2f00129-bfef-5325-bde1-618b368cc3e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435406} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9fa936b-ac16-50be-bf66-4d709c62af39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435410}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "37e33b7e-4ee9-510a-871b-336b8d3b6afc" :question/math-academy-id "q-16551" :question/problem "![](images/0f/0faaa905476ef6b6224a4b6b24ceb1adde4b14680507a7c6289885dce1bdd997.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(3,-1),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=3,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{25} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372460 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087834 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6f8f8ef-20d2-5810-a5a5-d20ce3111b82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6f8f8ef-20d2-5810-a5a5-d20ce3111b82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372462} :answer-field/id #uuid "1eee6fc9-216b-5f3c-bf2c-67ff272ef12f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372461} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5df0b774-b279-5fca-bfd2-36244b70e24a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5df0b774-b279-5fca-bfd2-36244b70e24a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372464} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcb83395-9403-5f77-b5d8-49ecf80f042e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372463}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ea506366-210c-5fd2-83b0-b52d9cd95147" :question/math-academy-id "q-277198" :question/problem "The center of the ellipse $\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{36}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{4}=1$ is located at the point$\\,($\n{{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=1$ and $k=-5,$ so the center is located at $(1,-5).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435412 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087834 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3f59427-ac1e-50ef-acc4-d78e93f3f6e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3f59427-ac1e-50ef-acc4-d78e93f3f6e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435404} :answer-field/id #uuid "b031b2ca-8ddc-558b-9ad0-2ad9d8032cd4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435409} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef66999e-c08f-54f1-a91f-420a161eba45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef66999e-c08f-54f1-a91f-420a161eba45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435405} :answer-field/