-academy-id "q-278482" :question/problem "![](images/19/19611e305d49d136f0a79189773b712243ec12f957fe16efca22ec2812393bd8.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(0,-2),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=5,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-0)^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373111 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087832 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "19d1448c-d5fd-5615-b657-ff4d66867834" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56a80b40-83c9-5a0c-b8de-49c06e672fc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373113} {:answer/id #uuid "2d6ecce1-0166-520e-8732-da9a869f6972" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373114} {:answer/id #uuid "490d76a9-1c74-52a1-970d-53ccf9e78a74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373115} {:answer/id #uuid "dfc9510a-1fe8-5c2a-8999-5d24f75e147e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373116} {:answer/id #uuid "01dfe7f3-e59a-58b3-98eb-dce687463c7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfc9510a-1fe8-5c2a-8999-5d24f75e147e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373116} :answer-field/id #uuid "884e0837-dc25-582c-8453-afd1b56b7ce5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373112}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b374a71-3074-56e8-acde-79803b53ed1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-70478" :question/problem "![](images/83/832adca41a55ffa7018ac5a2ea32d63a7ff37a545dc33fa88f13fbc9495b698a.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(1,2),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=3,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435414 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087832 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "19d1448c-d5fd-5615-b657-ff4d66867834" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "442cd84d-41ff-5be9-a6